      "answer": "At the end of Chapter 2, the animals returned to the farm buildings and were hesitant to enter the farmhouse, which they preserved as a museum without living in it. Snowball and Napoleon renamed the farm from Manor Farm to Animal Farm by painting the name on the gate. They also inscribed the Seven Commandments of Animalism on the barn wall as an unalterable law for all animals to follow. The animals agreed to these commandments and began learning them by heart. They then prepared to start the hay harvest, although concerns arose about the large amount of milk produced by the cows, which mysteriously disappeared while the animals were working. Thus, the chapter ended with the animals beginning the harvest and the missing milk noted.",
