      "answer": "At the beginning of Chapter II, three nights after old Major's death, the animals on the farm begin to secretly organize and prepare for a future Rebellion inspired by Major's speech. The pigs, recognized as the smartest animals, especially Snowball, Napoleon, and Squealer, take the lead in developing the teachings into a system called Animalism. They hold secret meetings to teach the other animals, meeting some resistance and questions, particularly from Mollie the mare and from the tales of Moses the raven about Sugarcandy Mountain. Despite difficulties, some animals like Boxer and Clover become faithful disciples attending all meetings. Meanwhile, Mr. Jones, the farmer, is neglectful and disheartened, contributing to the deteriorating condition of the farm, setting the stage for the Rebellion to occur sooner than expected.",
